WEBVTT

00:00:01.880 --> 00:00:05.620
It's Sunday, and this is the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:10.180
Here's your day in Microsoft updates, in 3 minutes flat.

00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:17.870
On the same page: this week's best. Soon,

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:21.510
Teams lets you pop out a sign language interpreter.

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:25.850
Their video stays in view while you share or switch layouts.

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:37.210
In class, Teams will let meeting organizers decide who can use Copilot and AI,

00:00:37.210 --> 00:00:38.090
due January.

00:00:39.380 --> 00:00:44.690
Got Teams Rooms Pro? A shared countdown timer for the room is due in January.

00:00:46.410 --> 00:00:52.280
Edge 158 is out: switch workspaces in one window, and pin them with an emoji.

00:00:53.910 --> 00:00:56.780
Its new Remix lets you restyle supported pages w

00:00:56.780 --> 00:00:59.720
ith built-in controls or plain-language requests.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:01.630
For university AI labs,

00:01:01.630 --> 00:01:06.710
Foundry's Programmed Training is in preview: your code, Foundry's GPUs.

00:01:07.500 --> 00:01:09.560
Your Python decides what to sample,

00:01:09.560 --> 00:01:12.380
how to score it and when to update the weights.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.810
Building a student help agent?

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:21.270
Foundry can now test whole conversations, not single answers, in preview.

00:01:22.500 --> 00:01:27.600
School IT? Exchange's High Volume Email will also reach outside addresses,

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:29.250
previewing in December.

00:01:30.000 --> 00:01:35.940
A Cornell and LSU team won $200,000 from Microsoft's Quantum Pioneers Program.

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:40.380
And Microsoft's AI Transparency Initiative,

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:44.740
with over 40 organisations, aims to make agents easier to audit.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.050
The fine print?

00:01:46.050 --> 00:01:51.270
Teams' live AI interpreter for webinars is now due February, not December.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:56.980
And the Azure Functions OpenAI extension loses support next April,

00:01:56.980 --> 00:01:58.280
so plan your move.

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:06.650
After hours, Insiders get full stereo on Bluetooth LE Audio earbuds,

00:02:06.650 --> 00:02:08.200
even with the mic on.

00:02:09.380 --> 00:02:11.200
There's a new People widget too,

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:14.220
to jump back into chats from Phone Link or WhatsApp.

00:02:16.880 --> 00:02:20.530
And this weekend, Game Pass members can try Polterguys,

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.650
a ghostly party game for eight.

00:02:23.910 --> 00:02:29.440
Shared timers, a visible interpreter, clear AI rules: everyone on the same page.

00:02:30.000 --> 00:02:32.350
Zoom out, and it never stops shipping.

00:02:33.750 --> 00:02:36.620
Some of it's shipped. The rest is on its way.

00:02:37.500 --> 00:02:40.880
One day, all of this. Tomorrow, probably more.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:47.870
You've been watching the Microsoft for Education Daily.

00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.940
See you tomorrow.
